node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# The nexus cache (docs/spec/05-nexus.md §1.3): DERIVED perception of the tree, rebuildable
# at will with `gwtp nexus build`, authoritative for nothing. Committed derived bytes would
# drift from the tree that derives them within one commit — so they never land in the tree.
# (Deliberately narrower than `.gwtp/`: whether `.gwtp/proposals/` is committed is an open
# governance question, OPEN-QUESTIONS.md Q-53, and an ignore rule must not answer it.)
.gwtp/nexus/

# NOT ignored, and easy to miss: package-lock.json MUST be committed.
# `npm ci` — what CONTRIBUTING.md documents as the one fresh-clone command, and what every CI
# job runs — fails outright without a lockfile. It is named here as a comment precisely because
# a reader scanning .gitignore for "what does not get committed" is the reader most likely to
# leave it untracked.
